{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>On the eighth day.</b> It seemed to us that 'on the eighth day' is the eighth of Nisan, for the Tabernacle was erected on the first of the month. But the transmitters said that it was Rosh Chodesh Nisan, and during the seven days of ordination Moses would erect the Tabernacle each day and dismantle it, in order to train in it and to teach." "<b>Moses called to Aaron and to his sons.</b> And they came out from the entrance of the Tent of Meeting, or the assembly entered the court."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {0 "Resolved המעתיקים as 'the transmitters,' i.e., rabbinic tradition handed down."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:09:10.330195203Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}